@Article(time: 3) {
    @Intro(title: "SymbolPicker Fundamentals Review") {
        Celebrate the core milestones of the Checker project, where you established a robust foundation for a multiplatform app using the SymbolPicker Framework. Prepare for future chapters to enhance your app with advanced interactivity and multiplatform support.
        @Image(source: DDM-Banner, alt: "SwiftData file icon.")
    }
    
    ## Summary
    Congratulations on completing Chapter 1 of the Checker project! You’ve built a solid foundation for a multiplatform application using the SymbolPicker Framework, creating an intuitive app that supports dynamic SF Symbol management. This milestone equips you with essential skills to expand in upcoming chapters with features like advanced UI interactions, search capabilities, and multiplatform optimization.

    Here’s a recap of the key achievements and skills you’ve acquired in Chapter 1:

    - **Project Setup and Integration**: Set up a new Xcode project for the Checker app and seamlessly integrated the SymbolPicker Framework via Swift Package Manager, configuring it for a multiplatform environment (Section: "Creating a Project").
    - **Data Model Design**: Established a well-organized file structure and developed robust data models, including a `Type` class with support for `Identifiable`, `Equatable`, `Comparable`, and `Hashable` for categorization, and an `Event` class with properties for event management, conforming to `Identifiable`, `Codable`, `Comparable`, and `Equatable` (Section: "Defining Data Models").
    - **File Organization**: Created a clear file hierarchy with `Type.swift` and `Event.swift`, ensuring maintainability and scalability for future development (Section: "Establishing File Organization Structure").
    - **SwiftData Integration**: Leveraged SwiftData with the `@Model` macro to define persistent data models, enabling efficient data management and relationships between `Type` and `Event` models (Section: "Building the Type Data Model" and "Building the Event Data Model").

    With these accomplishments, you’ve laid a strong foundation for a feature-rich SymbolPicker application. In upcoming chapters, you’ll explore advanced SymbolPicker capabilities, such as dynamic UI development, search functionality, and platform-specific optimizations for iOS, iPadOS, macOS, and visionOS, to create a more engaging and versatile user experience.
}
